# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2024), chunk 4. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Accursed Act": ["Wisdom save or the target takes 1d8 plus your casting modifier Psychic damage each turn it attacks or casts a spell.",
 "A creature you see in range makes a Wisdom save or is cursed for the duration. A cursed creature takes Psychic damage equal to 1d8 plus your spellcasting modifier when it makes an attack roll or casts a spell, once per turn. The spell ends early if the target neither attacks nor casts a spell during its turn. Higher levels: +1d8 per slot level above 1."],
"Antiballistics Field": ["A 40-ft Emanation jams ranged weapons, and projectiles passing through get Disadvantage and half damage.",
 "A 40-ft Emanation around you disrupts missile fire. Any ranged weapon used for an attack inside it malfunctions and the attack is lost. A jammed weapon cannot attack until a creature uses the Utilize action to fix it. Attacks whose projectiles merely pass through the Emanation have Disadvantage and deal half damage on a hit."],
"Ballistic Smite": ["Bonus Action on a hit: the target takes 2d6 extra damage of Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder type.",
 "Cast right after you hit with an attack. Pick Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. The target takes an extra 2d6 damage of that type. The attack itself can deal either its normal damage type or the chosen one, your choice. Higher levels: +1d6 per slot level above 1."],
"Burning Blade": ["Make a melee attack using your casting ability. It can deal Fire damage, and max dice explode up to your modifier.",
 "Wreathe the weapon in flame and make one melee attack with it, using your spellcasting ability for the attack and damage rolls. A hit can deal Fire damage or the weapon's usual type. When the weapon's damage die or a spell die shows its highest value, roll it again and add the result, repeating on further maximums, with a cap of extra dice equal to your spellcasting modifier. Cantrip scaling: extra Fire damage of 1d6 at level 5, 2d6 at 11, 3d6 at 17."],
"Clue": ["Ritual. Footprints and fingerprints in a 30-ft Emanation glow for 10 minutes, each creature in its own color.",
 "Footprints and fingerprints within a 30-ft Emanation around you glow faintly for the duration. When you cast it, pick a moment up to 10 days back. Only prints left from then until now are shown. Each creature gets its own color but is not identified. Anyone who moves or touches things in the area afterward leaves colored prints too, which can expose invisible creatures."],
"Consecrated Armor": ["Ritual. 8 hours: your base AC is 12 + Dex, and you add your casting modifier to AC against Aberrations, Fey, Fiends and Undead.",
 "You trace a holy sign on yourself to raise an unseen barrier. Your base AC becomes 12 plus your Dexterity modifier. Against attacks from Aberrations, Fey, Fiends or Undead you also add your spellcasting modifier to AC. The spell ends early if you put on armor."],
"Curse Object": ["Ritual. Touch an unattended object up to 5 ft across. It becomes a cursed, attunement-requiring item with a chosen curse.",
 "You curse an unworn, uncarried object that fits in a 5-ft cube. Until the spell ends it becomes magical, requires attunement and is cursed. The curse shows only through Identify or on attunement, and then extends to the attuned creature. Pick one curse. Bleeding: cannot regain HP. Frenzied (weapons only): dealing damage with it makes the wielder Frenzied for 1 minute, so it treats everyone as an enemy, picks attack and spell targets at random among creatures it sees in range, and must make an Opportunity Attack when able. Hobbled: Speed halved and no Dash. Obsessed: the creature will not part with it, and has Disadvantage on other weapons if the object is a weapon. Restless: after a Long Rest it must pass a Constitution save or gain no benefit. Speechless: cannot speak. Unfortunate: a natural 20 on a D20 Test becomes a 1. Vulnerable: Vulnerability to one damage type chosen at casting."],
"Curse of Blades": ["Wisdom save or the target is Frenzied, attacking random creatures. It repeats the save at each turn end.",
 "A creature you see in range makes a Wisdom save or is cursed and Frenzied for the duration. A Frenzied creature cannot tell friend from foe and treats all creatures it sees as enemies. It picks targets for attacks, spells and abilities at random among creatures it sees in range, and must make an Opportunity Attack if anyone provokes one. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the save and ends the spell on a success."],
"Defenestration": ["Strength save or the target is thrown 20 ft through a window, taking 4d6 Slashing and falling Prone.",
 "A wave of force flings a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Strength save. On a failure it is pushed up to 20 ft through a window you choose. If no window is within 20 ft, a force window forms behind it and shatters once it passes. It takes 4d6 Slashing damage and is Prone after going through. On a success it is pushed only 10 ft and takes no damage. Higher levels: +1d6 damage and +5 ft push (on failure or success) per slot level above 2."],
"Divine Wrath": ["10-ft radius, 120 ft: Constitution save for 4d10 Necrotic or Radiant, half on a save. Kills turn to salt.",
 "You drop a mote of wrath on a point you see in range. Creatures you choose in a 10-ft-radius Sphere there make a Constitution save, taking 4d10 Necrotic or Radiant damage (your pick) on a failure, or half on a success. A creature reduced to 0 HP is disintegrated into salt, and its gear falls in its space. Only True Resurrection or Wish can revive it. Higher levels: +1d10 per slot level above 3."],
"Exhume": ["Ritual. A pile of Humanoid bones rises in a 20-ft square. In a burial place, 1d4 corpses or bone piles appear.",
 "Pick an unoccupied 20-ft square on the ground within range. One pile of Humanoid bones rises from it. If you cast this in a graveyard, mausoleum, barrow or similar burial site, 1d4 corpses or bone piles come up instead. The ground is not disturbed, the bones simply appear."],
"Finger Guns": ["Bonus Action: your hand is a Simple Ranged weapon (60/240 ft, Slow) dealing 2d6 Force using your casting ability.",
 "For 1 minute your extended finger and thumb count as a Simple Ranged weapon with range 60/240 ft and the Slow mastery. You can attack with your spellcasting ability instead of Dexterity. A hit deals 2d6 Force damage and does not add the ability modifier. Cantrip scaling: range grows by 30/120 ft at level 5 (90/360), 11 (120/480) and 17 (150/600)."],
"Force Buckler": ["Bonus Action: +2 AC until your next turn while you hold no Shield. Ends if you are hit.",
 "A translucent field of force springs from your gauntlet. Until the start of your next turn you gain +2 AC if you are not wielding a Shield. The spell ends early if an attack hits you."],
"Frenzy": ["20-ft radius, 120 ft: Wisdom save or Frenzied (attack random creatures) for up to 1 minute.",
 "Each creature in a 20-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point in range makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frenzied for the duration. A Frenzied creature treats all creatures it sees as enemies, picks targets for attacks, spells and abilities at random among those it sees in range, and must make an Opportunity Attack when anyone provokes one. At the end of each of its turns it repeats the save, ending the condition on a success."],
"Gahoul's Scapegoat": ["Touch a willing creature for 8 hours. Reaction when you are hit: swap places with it within 60 ft so it takes the hit. Spell ends.",
 "Over 1 minute you mark a willing creature you touch with an arcane symbol. If an attack roll hits you during the 8 hours while the marked creature is within 60 ft, you can use your Reaction to teleport and swap places with it, so the attack hits it instead. The spell then ends."],
"Geomantic Discernment": ["Ritual, Concentration up to 10 minutes. You see an aura on valuable metals, gems and ores in a 60-ft Emanation, through any nonmagical material.",
 "You sense valuable minerals in a 60-ft Emanation around you. For the duration, valuable metals, gems, ores, native elements and similar resources in the area glow with an aura only you see. You see the glow through any amount of nonmagical material."],
"Hangover": ["Constitution save: 3d8 Psychic and Poisoned until your next turn end, half damage on a save. Disadvantage on Concentration from it.",
 "A drunken aura washes over a creature you choose within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 3d8 Psychic damage and is Poisoned until the end of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage and no Poisoned. The target has Disadvantage on Constitution saves to hold Concentration because of this damage. Higher levels: +1d8 per slot level above 2."],
"Hex: Blood Curse": ["Constitution save. The cursed target drops to 0 HP if damaged to under 5 HP before your next turn ends. Threshold grows with level.",
 "A creature you see within 60 ft is cursed until the end of your next turn. If it takes damage while cursed and is left with fewer than 5 HP, it drops to 0 HP. Cantrip scaling: the threshold rises by 5 at level 5 (10 HP), 11 (15 HP) and 17 (20 HP). The listed save is Constitution."],
"Hex: Doomward": ["Touch: the first time the target would drop to 0 HP before your next turn ends, it drops to 1 HP instead. Once per 24 hours per target.",
 "You touch a willing creature. The first time it would drop to 0 HP before the spell ends at the end of your next turn, it instead stays at 1 HP and the spell ends. The spell has no effect on a target you already cast it on within the past 24 hours."],
"Hex: Garble": ["Charisma save or the target cannot speak coherently or cast spells with Verbal components until your next turn ends.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Charisma save. On a failure it cannot speak coherently and cannot cast spells that have a Verbal component until the spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Hex: Mire": ["30-ft Emanation of swamp becomes Difficult Terrain until your next turn ends. It does not slow you.",
 "The ground in a 30-ft Emanation around you turns to murky swamp. It is Difficult Terrain until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. This terrain costs you no extra movement."],
"Hex: Peacebond": ["30-ft Emanation locks weapons and ammo in their holders until your next turn ends. Utilize plus Athletics vs your DC frees one.",
 "A 30-ft Emanation around you locks weapons to their containers. Weapons and ammunition of every creature inside stay fixed in sheaths, quivers or holsters until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. A creature can use the Utilize action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, freeing an item on a success."],
"Hex: Sweet Tooth": ["Touch a loose nonmagical object up to 1-ft cube. It becomes candy until your next turn ends. Target is immune for 1 minute after.",
 "You touch a nonmagical object that is not worn or carried and fits in a 1-ft cube. It becomes an edible candy copy of your chosen kind, such as gingerbread, candy cane or licorice. If it is not eaten or destroyed when the spell ends at the end of your next turn, it returns to its original material. After the spell ends on a target, that target is immune to it for 1 minute."],
"Hocuspocus": ["Create a minor spooky effect for 1 minute. Up to three of its effects can be active at once.",
 "You conjure small paranormal effects. Pick one. Grave Mists: ground fog fills a 15-ft cube. Ominous Lights: candles, torches and open flames darken and flicker. Paranormal Chill: chill or warm the air in a 10-ft cube by 10 degrees. Poltergeist Activity: small unattended objects rattle or hover an inch up. Spirit Orbs: up to four fist-sized glowing orbs drift in range, giving only a dim glow. Spooky Noises: a quiet sound such as whispers, insects or crying comes from a point you choose in range. Each lasts 1 minute and you can keep up to three effects active."],
"Identity Curse": ["Touch, Wisdom save. A failed target sleeps 1 hour, then loses its personal memories until the spell ends (until dispelled).",
 "You touch a creature's temple and try to erase who it is. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is Unconscious for 1 hour and cursed to forget its identity. When it wakes it has lost all personal memories but keeps general knowledge, proficiencies and statistics. It does not realize it has class features, feats or magic and will not willingly use them unless it rediscovers them. Left alone, it soon takes a new name and starts a new life. When the spell ends, the memories return."],
"Instant Replay": ["Bonus Action when your attack misses: reset time and repeat the attack roll against the same target.",
 "As your attack misses, you rewind to the moment before it and make the attack roll again against the same target, which may hit this time."],
"Jam Weapon": ["Reaction, 60 ft: a targeted weapon malfunctions and its attack fails. It stays jammed until fixed with Utilize.",
 "The weapon you target malfunctions and the attack fails. A jammed weapon cannot make attacks until a creature uses the Utilize action to repair it."],
"Lightning Surge": ["5-ft Emanation: Dexterity save or 1d6 Lightning damage. Scales to 4d6.",
 "Lightning erupts around you. Each creature in a 5-ft Emanation must pass a Dexterity save or take 1d6 Lightning damage. Cantrip scaling: 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at 11, 4d6 at 17."],
"Mandy's Marvelous Dress": ["Touch: a ball gown that lets the wearer treat a Charisma D20 Test as a 10, and makes attackers save or miss. Lasts to midnight or 24 hours.",
 "A willing creature you touch is clothed in a perfectly tailored gown with glittering jewelry. It can sit over or replace the creature's outfit. The creature cannot remove the dress until the spell ends, and the jewelry vanishes if taken off. Elegant Flair: when the wearer makes a Charisma D20 Test, it can replace the number rolled with 10. Glamorous Ward: an attacker that sees the wearer must pass a Wisdom save or miss, and an attacker that succeeds is immune to this until the spell ends. Duration: where time passes normally, until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight, otherwise 24 hours. Then the dress vanishes in sparkles and the original clothes return."],
"Might of the Abyss": ["Concentration 1 minute: three other creatures in 15 ft deal an extra 1d4 Necrotic with weapon hits.",
 "You channel power from the Lower Planes into three creatures other than you within range. Whenever one of them deals damage with a weapon, it deals an extra 1d4 Necrotic damage. Higher levels: one more target per slot level above 1."],
"Paradox": ["Undo one action taken in range within the last round. The actor takes 10d8 Psychic damage.",
 "You twist time and erase one action of your choice taken within range during the last round. Its direct effects, such as damage from an attack or spell, are undone. Indirect effects, such as creatures choosing to move elsewhere, remain. Reality recoils, and the creature that took the action takes 10d8 Psychic damage."],
"Phantom Grapnel": ["Force chain and hook, 30 ft. Pull yourself to a space or Huge target, or pull a Large or smaller target 10 ft after a Strength save.",
 "You launch a chain and hook of force at a creature or empty space you see in range. If you target a space or a Huge or larger creature, the grapnel pulls you to it in a straight line, and you provoke Opportunity Attacks for this movement as usual. If you target a Large or smaller creature, it makes a Strength save or is pulled up to 10 ft toward you."],
"Prehensile Hair": ["Ritual, 8 hours: your hair grows up to 15 ft and acts as a reach extension for Touch spells, Help, Utilize and simple tasks.",
 "You grow any of your body hair up to 15 ft long, supernaturally tough, and use it to extend your reach for the duration. Through it you can cast Touch-range spells, take the Help or Utilize action, or do simple tasks out to 15 ft. It cannot wield weapons or a Shield, nor carry more than 10 lb. Your hair returns to normal length when the spell ends."],
"Proto-Divination": ["Pick one: Omen (GM omen), Premonition (symbolic vision, level 3+), or Portent (record a d20 to swap into a D20 Test, level 3+).",
 "Casting takes 1 minute. Pick one option, some of which need a minimum slot level. Omen: focus on a past event, present situation or planned course of action and the GM gives an omen that is secretly hopeful, baleful or neutral, with larger omens for bigger events. If you choose this more than once before a Long Rest, there is a 50 percent chance of a random omen. Premonition (level 3+ slot): the GM gives a symbolic vision of an event in the next 24 hours. You cannot use this option again until a Long Rest. Portent (level 3+ slot): roll 1d20 and record it. You can replace any D20 Test made by you or a creature you see with that number, choosing before the roll. The recorded number is lost after a Long Rest or if you use this option again."],
"Proto-Necromancy": ["Concentration 1 hour: raise an Undead servant from a table (Animal Skeleton, Skeleton, Zombie, up to Wight with higher slots).",
 "You animate an Undead servant. Pick a target and an Undead from the Proto-Necromancy table. It dies when the spell ends. It is your ally, shares your Initiative count and acts right after you, obeys verbal commands for free, and otherwise Dodges and uses its movement to avoid danger. It attacks with your spell attack modifier. Table by slot level, with required target: 1 Animal Skeleton (pile of Beast bones), 2 Skeleton (Humanoid bones) or Zombie (Medium or Small Humanoid corpse), 3 Ghoul (Medium or Small Humanoid corpse), Specter (Humanoid corpse dead no more than 1 hour) or Warhorse Skeleton (Large Beast bones), 4 Minotaur Skeleton (Giant or Monstrosity bones), 5 Ogre Zombie (Giant or Monstrosity corpse), 6 Mummy or Wight (Medium or Small Humanoid corpse). Higher slots allow stronger Undead, and Undead made this way cannot create more Undead."],
"Recall": ["Bonus Action: mark your spot. Until your next turn ends, Reaction to teleport back to it before an attack, spell or nearby move. Spell ends.",
 "You record your current location. Until the end of your next turn you can use your Reaction when an attack roll is made against you, a creature casts a spell, or a creature moves within 5 ft of you, to teleport back to the recorded spot, or the nearest free space if it is occupied. The teleport happens before the triggering attack or spell. The spell then ends."],
"Rumbling Charge": ["Move up to 30 ft in a line free, then a creature within 5 ft makes a Strength save or takes 2d12 Bludgeoning (half on save).",
 "You take on the power of a landslide and immediately move up to 30 ft in a straight line along the ground, using no movement and provoking no Opportunity Attacks. If you finish within 5 ft of a creature, it makes a Strength save, taking 2d12 Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. Higher levels: +1d12 per slot level above 1."],
"Scrutinize Foe": ["Bonus Action, 60 ft: learn two facts about a creature (AC, Speed, immunities, resistances, best or worst ability, active spells).",
 "You study one creature you see in range and learn two pieces of information of your choice from this list: Armor Class, Speed, Immunities, Resistances, highest ability score, lowest ability score, and enchantments (the spells currently affecting it). The GM must share the chosen facts."],
"Skirmish": ["Bonus Action, touch, 1 minute: a willing creature has doubled Speed, ignores Difficult Terrain and provokes no Opportunity Attacks.",
 "You boost the mobility of a willing creature you touch. For the duration its Speed is doubled, Difficult Terrain does not slow it, and it provokes no Opportunity Attacks."],
"Spark of Life": ["A corpse dead under an hour stands, moves 15 ft and attacks with your spell attack. Damage by size, d4 to d12. Scales with level.",
 "A jolt of necromantic energy briefly raises a corpse of a Huge or smaller creature that died within the last hour. It stands, moves up to 15 ft and makes one melee attack with your spell attack modifier against a target of your choice within its reach. A hit deals Bludgeoning damage by size: Tiny 1d4, Small 1d6, Medium 1d8, Large 1d10, Huge 1d12. After attacking it collapses again, and it does not become Undead. Cantrip scaling: one more damage die at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Sulfuric Smoke": ["5-ft cube at 60 ft: Constitution save or 1d8 Acid. The smoke lightly obscures and gives Disadvantage on attacks inside. Scales to 4d8.",
 "You make a 5-ft cube of acidic smoke at a point you see in range. Each creature in it must pass a Constitution save or take 1d8 Acid damage. The cube is Lightly Obscured by noxious fumes and lasts until the start of your next turn. A creature entirely inside has Disadvantage on attack rolls. Cantrip scaling: 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11, 4d8 at 17."],
"Séance": ["10-minute casting: you and three or more willing creatures call a spirit. It answers three questions during 1 minute.",
 "You and at least three willing creatures join hands and call a spirit to answer questions. Describe or name a creature familiar to you. If its soul is free and willing, it appears as a ghostly specter. The spell fails if that spirit was the target within the last 10 days. For the duration you can ask the specter up to three questions. It knows only what it knew in life, including languages. Answers tend to be brief, cryptic or repetitive, and it need not answer truthfully if you are hostile or it sees you as an enemy. There is a 5 percent chance you reach the wrong spirit, which answers untruthfully or ambiguously."],
"Unseen Artisan": ["Ritual, 8 hours: an Invisible force worker (AC 10, 1 HP) uses tools or crafts nonmagical items on your Bonus Action command.",
 "You create an Invisible, mindless, shapeless Medium force in an unoccupied space on the ground in range. It has AC 10, 1 HP and Strength 10, and cannot attack. If it drops to 0 HP the spell ends. Once on each of your turns, as a Bonus Action, you can command it to take the Utilize action with a set of tools in range or to craft a nonmagical item. It is proficient with all Artisan's Tools and performs tasks a skilled human worker could. You supply the tools and raw materials. If it needs an ability check it uses your spellcasting ability. If you order a task that would take it more than 60 ft from you, the spell ends."],
"Word of Control": ["Bonus Action, 30 ft: Wisdom save or Charmed until your next turn ends. You give it free commands and it obeys. 24-hour immunity on save.",
 "You speak a word of authority at a creature you see in range. It makes a Wisdom save or is Charmed until the end of your next turn. A creature you targeted with this spell in the last 24 hours passes automatically. While Charmed, the target neither moves nor acts unless you command it, and you can give orders for free, such as attack a creature, move somewhere or fetch an item. It does its best to obey on its turn."],
"Zephyr's Feather": ["Concentration 1 minute: four razor feathers orbit you. Cast and Bonus Action each turn: ranged spell attack for 1d8 Force at 120 ft.",
 "Four sharp alabaster feathers appear and orbit you for the duration. When you cast the spell, and as a Bonus Action on later turns, you can spend one feather to make a ranged spell attack against a creature you see within 120 ft. A hit deals 1d8 Force damage. Higher levels: +1d8 damage per slot level above 1."],
}
